---
/** Why we built Spenza. */
---

<section class="hm-sec hm-sec--white hm-position">
  <div class="hm-wrap">
    <div class="hm-position-grid hm-stack hm-reveal">
      <div>
        <div class="hm-eyebrow">WHY WE BUILT SPENZA</div>
        <p class="hm-position-lead">
          Connectivity should be <em>a line in your config</em>, not a year of your roadmap.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hm-position-copy">
        <p>
          Carriers built their systems for handsets and monthly consumer plans. Everything since
          &mdash; a sensor in a shipping container, a watch on a child, an agent answering a
          support line &mdash; has had to be bolted onto that model one contract at a time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Spenza exists so that work happens once, in one place, and every team that follows
          inherits it. That is the whole thesis, and it is why sourcing, cost, billing, and voice
          sit on a single data model rather than four products with a shared logo.
        </p>
        <a class="hm-underline" href="/about-us/">More about the company</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
